# PennyRouter settings — canonical template for every variable.
#
# Env layout (three files):
#   .env.example  this file: documents every variable (names only for
#                 secrets — never put real values here).
#   .env.dev      committed working values for dev (generic only).
#   .env          gitignored overlay, secrets + custom URLs only:
#                 BASETEN_API_KEY, MODAL_KEY_ID, MODAL_KEY_SECRET,
#                 RANKINGS_API_KEY, MODAL_BASE_URL, MODAL_JUDGE_URL,
#                 MODAL_MODELS, BASETEN_MODELS. Never commit it.
# Every variable has a sane default in the compose files, so a bare
# `docker compose up` works; `make dev` loads .env.dev plus .env.
#
# NOTE: gateway backend keys do NOT belong here — they travel with each
# request (see docs/api.md). The judge keys below are the only exception:
# they are read by the offline catalog process (never the gateway, never
# on the request path). Set real values in your local gitignored `.env`,
# never here.

# Port the gateway listens on inside the container.
PORT=8080
# Port published on the host for local dev (the proxy-reached server
# stack publishes no ports and ignores this).
HOST_PORT=3000
# Image reference. Dev compose tags its local build with this;
# prod compose pulls it from GitHub Packages (ghcr.io).
IMAGE=ghcr.io/lsk242/pennyrouter:latest
# Upstream base URL for POST /v1/chat/completions (Iter 1b).
# Native `/api/v1/…` paths compose against this base minus its trailing
# `/api` (Iter 25), so account/catalog reads reach OpenRouter intact.
OPENROUTER_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api
# Management writes through the fallback proxy (Iter 25): key creation,
# credit purchases, workspace budget changes. Unset (default) answers
# 403 without touching upstream; set to 1 to proxy them. Reads always
# proxy.
# ALLOW_MANAGEMENT_PROXY=
# Provider-pinned upstreams (Iter 16): `modal/<model>` and
# `baseten/<model>` forward there instead of OpenRouter, with the
# caller's Authorization forwarded unchanged (pure BYOK: no gateway
# keys on the serving path). Unset = that provider's routes fail
# closed with provider_not_configured. Baseten defaults to its public
# inference host; Modal has no shared deployment, so it stays unset
# until configured. Bases carry no `/v1` route prefix (the gateway
# appends the incoming `/v1/…` path itself; a trailing `/v1` is
# stripped, but leave it off).
# MODAL_BASE_URL=
# BASETEN_BASE_URL=https://inference.baseten.co
# Menu-nominated provider models (comma-separated, 1-3 ids each):
# advertised on GET /v1/models as modal/<id> / baseten/<id>, each
# only when its provider base above is configured. These are the
# operator's deployments/picks — the gateway never enumerates
# vendor catalogs itself.
# MODAL_MODELS=
# BASETEN_MODELS=
# Catalog artifact the gateway routes from (Iter 5): directory, manifest,
# or DB file. Empty/unset means plain passthrough without routing.
CATALOG_DB=/catalog
# Upstream concurrency bounds (Iter 9): max simultaneous upstream calls
# and max requests waiting for a slot; beyond both, shed with 503.
UPSTREAM_MAX_CONCURRENT=64
UPSTREAM_MAX_QUEUED=128
# Catalog reload cadence in seconds (Iter 10): 0 disables the background
# reload (load-once behavior).
RELOAD_INTERVAL_SECS=60
# Catalog sync image: local compose tags its build with this; server
# deploys pull it, so it must be a pullable tag (same deal as IMAGE).
CATALOG_IMAGE=ghcr.io/lsk242/pennyrouter-catalog:latest
# Seconds between catalog sync cycles (0 = run once and exit).
SYNC_INTERVAL=3600
# Catalog input: 1 = live OpenRouter fetch (Iter 18), 0 = baked
# fixtures (offline default).
FETCH_OPENROUTER=0
# Sync input/output paths (docker/catalog-entrypoint.sh overrides;
# defaults suit the compose mount layout, rarely changed):
# MODELS (models.json), ENDPOINTS_DIR (per-model endpoints bodies),
# OUT_DIR (published artifacts), TRENDS (trend input), ASSIST
# (rank-assist input), PROMOS (promo windows input).
# MODELS=/input/models.json
# ENDPOINTS_DIR=/input/endpoints
# OUT_DIR=/catalog
# TRENDS=/input/trends.json
# ASSIST=/input/rank-assist.json
# PROMOS=/input/promos.json
# Extra model ids (comma-separated, Iter 24): fetched individually
# even when the models list omits them (e.g. non-text-output scoring
# models like Respan Span, which back the `decision` tier).
EXTRA_MODEL_IDS=respan/span-01-lite:free
# Popularity pins for the gateway menu: an OpenRouter key for the
# public Data API (rankings-daily + app-rankings, trailing 7 days).
# Any valid key works; 2 calls per sync (far inside 30/min, 500/day).
# Empty/unset = sync publishes without pins (menu still serves the
# virtual ids + MODAL/BASETEN_MODELS). The same key also
# authenticates the OpenRouter judge leg (Iter 30). Key lives here
# like the judge keys — sync-time batch only, never on the request
# path.
# RANKINGS_API_KEY=
# OpenRouter judge model (Iter 30): which model
# `--judge-backend openrouter` judges with, e.g.
# "<vendor>/<model>" (any OpenRouter chat model id).
# Nothing pinned (models come and go): unset/empty =
# openrouter judging fails closed.
# OPENROUTER_JUDGE_MODEL=
# Catalog judge keys (Phase 4): live LLM backends for catalog-process
# judging. Empty/unset = judging stays on recorded fixtures.
# Baseten: workspace or federated key; OpenAI-compatible chat at
# https://inference.baseten.co/v1 (detail: docs/catalog-sync-roadmap.md).
BASETEN_API_KEY=
# Modal: proxy-token pair for the deployed judge endpoint (dashboard
# Settings -> proxy auth tokens), sent as Modal-Key / Modal-Secret.
MODAL_KEY_ID=
MODAL_KEY_SECRET=
# Modal judge endpoint URL (per-deployment, e.g.
# https://<workspace>--<app>-<fn>.modal.run). Required for Modal judging.
MODAL_JUDGE_URL=
# Decision-model catalog (Iter 15): pass --judges <file> to
# catalog-process to pick the judge model per backend plus the
# selection policy (sample rate, scope, call/spend caps). Recorded
# judging needs none of the keys above.
# Debug UIs (Iter 17): both off unless set to 1. GATEWAY_UI registers
# GET /ui on the gateway (same port); CATALOG_UI lets the catalog-ui
# browser start at all. No other effect when unset.
# GATEWAY_UI=
# CATALOG_UI=
# Smart classifier leg (Iter 26): enables openrouter/pair/smart[/max]
# (+ privacy variants). Unset CLASSIFIER_MODEL means those ids fail
# closed with classifier_not_configured; every other id keeps
# pure-local routing. No stored key, ever (Q08): the leg authenticates
# with the caller's Authorization header, optionally overridden
# per-request by x-pennyrouter-classifier-key. A foreign
# CLASSIFIER_BASE_URL therefore receives the caller's key by
# model-choice consent, like pinned routes. The leg always calls
# <base>/v1/chat/completions; a base ending in /v1 is accepted too
# (the suffix is stripped, never doubled).
# CLASSIFIER_MODEL=
# CLASSIFIER_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api
# CLASSIFIER_TIMEOUT_MS=8000
# CLASSIFIER_FALLBACK_TIER=low
# CLASSIFIER_MAX_TOKENS=64
# CLASSIFIER_MAX_INPUT_CHARS=32000
# Host port for the opt-in catalog-ui compose service
# (docker compose --profile ui up catalog-ui).
# CATALOG_UI_PORT=8080
# Docker network of the front reverse proxy (Nginx Proxy Manager):
# the server stack joins it so the proxy reaches gateway:8080 and
# catalog-ui:8080 with no published ports. Must already exist on the
# host (it belongs to the proxy stack). Local dev ignores it.
PROXY_NETWORK=nginx-proxy_default
